Here's a simplified single-file Java version of the same idea: an append-only event list, a surface of event numbers, replace instead of delete, building messages, and saving to a one-event-per-line file. It uses only the standard library and needs Java 17+.

```java
import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.util.*;

public class SessionDemo {

    /** One thing that happened. Never changed after it is added. */
    record Event(int seq, String type, String role, String text, List<Integer> replaces) {}

    /** A message as the LLM sees it. */
    record Message(String role, String text) {}

    static class Session {
        final List<Event> events = new ArrayList<>();   // the full log: append-only
        final List<Integer> surface = new ArrayList<>(); // seq numbers the model sees now

        /** Add a log-only event (turn start, markers...). The model never sees it. */
        Event log(String type) {
            Event e = new Event(events.size(), type, null, null, List.of());
            events.add(e);
            return e;
        }

        /** Add a visible message: goes into the log AND onto the surface. */
        Event append(String role, String text) {
            Event e = new Event(events.size(), "message", role, text, List.of());
            events.add(e);
            surface.add(e.seq());
            return e;
        }

        /**
         * Compaction / pruning: add a new event and swap a range of the surface
         * for it. The old events stay in the log; they are just no longer visible.
         */
        Event replace(int fromSeq, int toSeq, String role, String text) {
            int start = surface.indexOf(fromSeq);
            int end = surface.indexOf(toSeq);
            if (start < 0 || end < start) throw new IllegalArgumentException("range not on surface");

            List<Integer> replaced = new ArrayList<>(surface.subList(start, end + 1));
            Event e = new Event(events.size(), "message", role, text, replaced);
            events.add(e);

            surface.subList(start, end + 1).clear(); // drop the old seqs from the view
            surface.add(start, e.seq());             // put the new one in their place
            return e;
        }

        /** What gets sent to the LLM on every step: walk the surface, look up each event. */
        List<Message> deriveMessages() {
            List<Message> out = new ArrayList<>();
            for (int seq : surface) {
                Event e = events.get(seq);
                out.add(new Message(e.role(), e.text()));
            }
            return out;
        }

        /** Save the log: one event per line (the real code writes compressed JSONL). */
        void save(Path file) throws IOException {
            List<String> lines = new ArrayList<>();
            for (Event e : events) {
                lines.add(e.seq() + "\t" + e.type() + "\t" + e.role() + "\t" + escape(e.text())
                        + "\t" + e.replaces().toString().replaceAll("[\\[\\] ]", ""));
            }
            Files.write(file, lines);
        }

        /** Load: read the log back and REBUILD the surface by replaying the events. */
        static Session load(Path file) throws IOException {
            Session s = new Session();
            for (String line : Files.readAllLines(file)) {
                String[] p = line.split("\t", -1);
                List<Integer> replaces = new ArrayList<>();
                for (String n : p[4].split(",")) if (!n.isEmpty()) replaces.add(Integer.parseInt(n));
                String role = p[2].equals("null") ? null : p[2];
                Event e = new Event(Integer.parseInt(p[0]), p[1], role, unescape(p[3]), replaces);
                s.events.add(e);

                if (!e.type().equals("message")) continue;          // log-only event
                if (e.replaces().isEmpty()) { s.surface.add(e.seq()); continue; }
                int at = s.surface.indexOf(e.replaces().get(0));    // replay the replacement
                s.surface.removeAll(e.replaces());
                s.surface.add(at, e.seq());
            }
            return s;
        }

        static String escape(String t) { return t == null ? "null" : t.replace("\\", "\\\\").replace("\n", "\\n").replace("\t", "\\t"); }
        static String unescape(String t) {
            if (t.equals("null")) return null;
            StringBuilder b = new StringBuilder();
            for (int i = 0; i < t.length(); i++) {
                char c = t.charAt(i);
                if (c == '\\' && i + 1 < t.length()) {
                    char n = t.charAt(++i);
                    b.append(n == 'n' ? '\n' : n == 't' ? '\t' : n);
                } else b.append(c);
            }
            return b.toString();
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        Session s = new Session();
        s.log("turn/start");
        Event first = s.append("user", "fix the bug in a.ts");
        s.append("assistant", "calling grep");
        s.append("tool", "src/a.ts:12  const x = y +");      // a tool result
        Event last = s.append("assistant", "found it, editing");
        s.append("user", "also add a test");

        System.out.println("Before compaction:");
        s.deriveMessages().forEach(m -> System.out.println("  " + m));

        // Compaction: summarize everything from `first` to `last`.
        s.replace(first.seq(), last.seq(), "user",
                "<compacted-summary>User asked to fix a bug in src/a.ts line 12; fix in progress.</compacted-summary>");

        System.out.println("\nAfter compaction (what the LLM sees):");
        s.deriveMessages().forEach(m -> System.out.println("  " + m));

        System.out.println("\nThe log still has all " + s.events.size() + " events; surface = " + s.surface);

        Path file = Path.of("session.log");
        s.save(file);
        Session reloaded = Session.load(file);
        System.out.println("\nReloaded surface = " + reloaded.surface + " (same as before: "
                + reloaded.surface.equals(s.surface) + ")");
    }
}
```

**How it maps to the harness:**

| Java | Harness |
|---|---|
| `events` list | `session.events` (append-only log) |
| `surface` list of seqs | `session.surface.nodes` |
| `append()` | `session.append(..., { surfaceOp: 'append' })` |
| `replace()` + `replaces` | `surfaceOp: { op: 'replace' }` + `sourceEventSeqs` |
| `deriveMessages()` | `session.deriveMessages()`, run before every LLM call |
| `save()` / `load()` | the JSONL session file, replayed on resume |

To run it: `javac SessionDemo.java && java SessionDemo`. You'll see 5 messages before compaction and 2 after (the summary plus the newest user message). The log still holds all 7 events, and reloading the file rebuilds the same surface.
